<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover">
<style>
  :root{color-scheme:light;padding-top:env(safe-area-inset-top,0px);padding-bottom:env(safe-area-inset-bottom,0px);}
  body{margin:0;font:14px system-ui,-apple-system,"Segoe UI",Roboto,sans-serif;}
  img{max-width:100%;}
  [hidden]{display:none!important;}
</style>
<title>BRV Early Warning</title>
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Archivo:wght@500;600;700&family=Source+Sans+3:ital,wght@0,400;0,600;1,400&family=IBM+Plex+Mono:wght@400;500;600&display=swap">

<style>
/* Layout: single measured column on a cool paper ground; one full-width figure
   breaks the measure; staged content carries a numbered left rail. */
:root{
  --paper:#EEF1F4;
  --surface:#FFFFFF;
  --sunk:#E3E8ED;
  --ink:#13181D;
  --soft:#555F6A;
  --line:#CBD3DA;
  --accent:#13686A;
  --wash:rgba(19,104,106,.07);
  --warn:#94600F;
  --warn-wash:rgba(148,96,15,.10);
  --crit:#9A3729;
  --ok:#2C6840;

  --display:"Archivo","Helvetica Neue",Arial,sans-serif;
  --body:"Source Sans 3",-apple-system,"Segoe UI",Roboto,sans-serif;
  --mono:"IBM Plex Mono",ui-monospace,"SFMono-Regular",Menlo,monospace;
}
@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark){
  :root:not([data-theme="light"]){
    --paper:#0D1114; --surface:#161B20; --sunk:#1E252B;
    --ink:#E4E9ED; --soft:#96A0AA; --line:#2B333A;
    --accent:#4FB9B4; --wash:rgba(79,185,180,.12);
    --warn:#D9A245; --warn-wash:rgba(217,162,69,.14);
    --crit:#DE7764; --ok:#62AC79;
    color-scheme:dark;
  }
}
:root[data-theme="dark"]{
  --paper:#0D1114; --surface:#161B20; --sunk:#1E252B;
  --ink:#E4E9ED; --soft:#96A0AA; --line:#2B333A;
  --accent:#4FB9B4; --wash:rgba(79,185,180,.12);
  --warn:#D9A245; --warn-wash:rgba(217,162,69,.14);
  --crit:#DE7764; --ok:#62AC79;
  color-scheme:dark;
}

body{
  background:var(--paper);
  color:var(--ink);
  font-family:var(--body);
  font-size:16px;
  line-height:1.62;
  -webkit-font-smoothing:antialiased;
}
.wrap{max-width:860px;margin:0 auto;padding-inline:20px;padding-block:44px 72px;}
.full{max-width:1180px;margin:0 auto;padding-inline:20px;}

h1,h2,h3,h4{font-family:var(--display);text-wrap:balance;margin:0;line-height:1.18;letter-spacing:-.015em;}
h1{font-size:clamp(30px,5.4vw,46px);font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-.028em;}
h2{font-size:clamp(21px,3.2vw,27px);font-weight:600;}
h3{font-size:17px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-.005em;}
h4{font-size:14px;font-weight:600;}
p{margin:0;}

.eyebrow{
  font-family:var(--mono);font-size:11px;font-weight:500;
  letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--accent);
}
.rule{height:1px;background:var(--line);border:0;margin:0;}

section{margin-top:58px;}
.sechead{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:8px;margin-bottom:22px;}
.sechead .kicker{
  font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10.5px;letter-spacing:.14em;
  text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--soft);
}
.lede{color:var(--soft);font-size:16.5px;max-width:62ch;}
.stack{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:16px;}
.stack-sm{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:10px;}

/* ---------- masthead ---------- */
.mast{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:18px;}
.standfirst{font-size:19px;line-height:1.52;max-width:58ch;color:var(--ink);}
.meta{
  display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px 28px;
  font-family:var(--mono);font-size:11.5px;color:var(--soft);
  padding-top:16px;border-top:1px solid var(--line);
}
.meta b{color:var(--ink);font-weight:500;}

/* ---------- the ask ---------- */
.ask{
  background:var(--surface);border:1px solid var(--accent);
  border-left:4px solid var(--accent);
  padding:24px 26px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:12px;
}
.ask .tag{
  font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10.5px;letter-spacing:.14em;
  text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--accent);
}
.ask p{max-width:60ch;}
.ask .big{font-family:var(--display);font-size:21px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.3;}

/* ---------- guarantee cards ---------- */
.grid2{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:14px;}
.grid3{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:14px;}
@media (max-width:640px){.grid2,.grid3{grid-template-columns:1fr;}}
.card{
  background:var(--surface);border:1px solid var(--line);
  padding:18px 18px 20px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:7px;min-width:0;
}
.card .no{
  font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10.5px;letter-spacing:.12em;color:var(--accent);
}
.card p{font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.55;color:var(--soft);}

/* ---------- figure ---------- */
figure{margin:0;}
.figscroll{overflow-x:auto;background:var(--surface);border:1px solid var(--line);padding:18px 16px;}
.figscroll svg{display:block;width:100%;min-width:1040px;height:auto;}
.figscroll.narrow svg{min-width:560px;}
.figlegend{
  display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px 22px;margin-top:12px;
  font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10.5px;color:var(--soft);
}
.figlegend span{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:7px;}
.sw{width:22px;height:11px;border:1.4px solid var(--line);background:var(--surface);flex:none;}
.sw.k{border-color:var(--ink);border-width:1.8px;}
.sw.ai{border-color:var(--accent);border-style:dashed;background:var(--wash);}
.sw.hm{border-color:var(--line);background:var(--sunk);}
figcaption{
  margin-top:12px;font-size:14px;color:var(--soft);max-width:70ch;
}
.scrollhint{
  font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10.5px;color:var(--soft);
  margin-top:8px;display:none;
}
@media (max-width:900px){.scrollhint{display:block;}}

svg text{font-family:var(--body);}
.n{fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--line);stroke-width:1.4;}
.nk{fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--ink);stroke-width:1.8;}
.ai{fill:var(--wash);stroke:var(--accent);stroke-width:1.4;stroke-dasharray:5 4;}
.hum{fill:var(--sunk);stroke:var(--line);stroke-width:1.4;}
.absent{fill:none;stroke:var(--line);stroke-width:1.4;stroke-dasharray:4 5;}
.tmid{fill:var(--soft);font-size:12px;text-anchor:middle;}
.tnow{fill:var(--ink);font-size:12px;text-anchor:middle;}
.t{fill:var(--ink);font-size:13px;text-anchor:middle;}
.tb{fill:var(--ink);font-size:13px;font-weight:600;text-anchor:middle;}
.ta{fill:var(--accent);font-size:13px;font-weight:600;text-anchor:middle;}
.ts{fill:var(--soft);font-size:10px;font-family:var(--mono);text-anchor:middle;}
.a{stroke:var(--soft);stroke-width:1.5;fill:none;}
.ad{stroke:var(--accent);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-dasharray:4 4;}
.as{stroke:var(--accent);stroke-width:1.6;fill:none;}
.bnd{stroke:var(--soft);stroke-width:1;stroke-dasharray:2 6;fill:none;}
.lbl{fill:var(--soft);font-size:9.5px;font-family:var(--mono);}
.lbla{fill:var(--accent);font-size:9.5px;font-family:var(--mono);}
.cap{fill:var(--soft);font-size:10px;font-family:var(--mono);letter-spacing:.12em;}
.capa{fill:var(--accent);font-size:10px;font-family:var(--mono);letter-spacing:.12em;}

/* ---------- metric table ---------- */
.tblwrap{overflow-x:auto;border:1px solid var(--line);background:var(--surface);}
table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:14.5px;min-width:520px;}
table.steps{min-width:820px;}
table.steps td:first-child{font-weight:600;}
th,td{text-align:left;padding:11px 14px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);vertical-align:top;}
th{
  font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10.5px;letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase;
  color:var(--soft);font-weight:500;background:var(--sunk);
}
tbody tr:last-child td{border-bottom:0;}
td.num{font-family:var(--mono);font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;white-space:nowrap;}
.tbd{
  font-family:var(--mono);font-size:12px;color:var(--soft);
  border-bottom:1px dotted var(--soft);
}

/* ---------- ladder ---------- */
.ladder{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:0;}
.rung{
  display:grid;grid-template-columns:62px minmax(0,1fr);gap:0;
  border-left:2px solid var(--line);
}
.rung:last-child{border-left-color:transparent;}
.rung .rail{position:relative;padding-top:22px;}
.rung .dot{
  position:absolute;left:-9px;top:24px;width:16px;height:16px;border-radius:50%;
  background:var(--paper);border:2px solid var(--accent);
}
.rung.opt .dot{border-color:var(--soft);}
.rung .stg{
  font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10.5px;letter-spacing:.1em;color:var(--soft);
  padding-left:18px;padding-top:1px;
}
.rung .body{padding:18px 0 30px;min-width:0;}
.rung h3{margin-bottom:4px;}
.rung .dur{
  font-family:var(--mono);font-size:11px;color:var(--accent);margin-bottom:10px;
}
.rung.opt .dur{color:var(--soft);}
.rowlist{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:7px;margin-top:4px;}
.row{display:grid;grid-template-columns:118px minmax(0,1fr);gap:12px;font-size:14.5px;}
@media (max-width:560px){.row{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:2px;}}
.row dt{
  font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10.5px;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;
  color:var(--soft);padding-top:4px;
}
@media (max-width:560px){.row dt{padding-top:6px;}}
.row dd{margin:0;color:var(--ink);}
.gate{
  margin-top:12px;background:var(--wash);border:1px solid var(--accent);
  padding:10px 13px;font-size:14px;display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:4px 10px;align-items:baseline;
}
.gate b{
  font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;
  color:var(--accent);font-weight:600;
}
.rung.opt .gate{background:transparent;border-color:var(--line);}
.rung.opt .gate b{color:var(--soft);}

/* ---------- workbench mock ---------- */
.mock{
  background:var(--surface);border:1px solid var(--line);
  font-family:var(--mono);font-size:12.5px;line-height:1.6;
}
.mock .bar{
  background:var(--sunk);border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);
  padding:9px 14px;display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:6px 16px;
  font-size:10.5px;letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--soft);
}
.mock .bar b{color:var(--ink);font-weight:600;}
.mock .inner{padding:16px 14px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:14px;}
.kv{display:grid;grid-template-columns:132px minmax(0,1fr);gap:4px 12px;}
@media (max-width:520px){.kv{grid-template-columns:1fr;}}
.kv dt{color:var(--soft);}
.kv dd{margin:0;color:var(--ink);}
.score{
  display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:10px;flex-wrap:wrap;
  border-top:1px solid var(--line);border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);
  padding:12px 0;
}
.score .v{
  font-family:var(--display);font-size:30px;font-weight:700;color:var(--warn);
  font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;letter-spacing:-.02em;
}
.score .lab{font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--soft);}
.reasons{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:6px;}
.reason{display:grid;grid-template-columns:18px minmax(0,1fr);gap:10px;}
.reason .b{color:var(--accent);}
.decide{
  background:var(--sunk);padding:11px 13px;
  font-size:11.5px;color:var(--soft);display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:6px 14px;
}
.decide b{color:var(--ink);}

/* ---------- objections ---------- */
.vs{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:14px;margin-top:16px;}
@media (max-width:640px){.vs{grid-template-columns:1fr;}}
.vs .col{border:1px solid var(--line);background:var(--surface);padding:18px;min-width:0;}
.vs .col.now{border-left:3px solid var(--warn);}
.vs .col.next{border-left:3px solid var(--accent);}
.vs .col h4{
  font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10.5px;letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;
  color:var(--soft);margin-bottom:12px;
}
.tl{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:9px;}
.tl .ev{display:grid;grid-template-columns:52px minmax(0,1fr);gap:12px;font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.5;}
.tl .ev time{
  font-family:var(--mono);font-size:11.5px;color:var(--soft);
  font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;padding-top:3px;
}
.obj{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:0;border-top:1px solid var(--line);}
.qa{
  display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) minmax(0,1.5fr);gap:10px 26px;
  padding:16px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);
}
@media (max-width:680px){.qa{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:6px;}}
.qa .q{font-family:var(--display);font-weight:600;font-size:15.5px;line-height:1.4;}
.qa .q::before{content:"“";color:var(--soft);}
.qa .q::after{content:"”";color:var(--soft);}
.qa .ans{font-size:14.5px;color:var(--soft);}
.qa .ans strong{color:var(--ink);font-weight:600;}

/* ---------- path ---------- */
.path{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:12px;counter-reset:p;}
.step{
  display:grid;grid-template-columns:30px minmax(0,1fr);gap:14px;
  padding-bottom:12px;border-bottom:1px dashed var(--line);
}
.step:last-child{border-bottom:0;}
.step .n2{
  font-family:var(--mono);font-size:12px;color:var(--accent);padding-top:3px;
  font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;
}
.step h4{margin-bottom:2px;}
.step p{font-size:14.5px;color:var(--soft);}

ul.tight{margin:0;padding-left:18px;}
ul.tight li{margin-bottom:5px;font-size:15px;}
ul.tight li::marker{color:var(--accent);}

.note{
  font-family:var(--mono);font-size:11.5px;line-height:1.7;color:var(--soft);
  border:1px dashed var(--line);padding:14px 16px;
}
.note b{color:var(--ink);font-weight:500;}
a{color:var(--accent);text-decoration-thickness:1px;text-underline-offset:2px;}
a:focus-visible,button:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--accent);outline-offset:2px;}
.src{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:12px;}
.srcitem{
  display:grid;grid-template-columns:132px minmax(0,1fr);gap:6px 20px;
  padding-bottom:12px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);
}
@media (max-width:620px){.srcitem{grid-template-columns:1fr;}}
.srcitem:last-child{border-bottom:0;}
.srcitem .who{
  font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10.5px;letter-spacing:.06em;text-transform:uppercase;
  color:var(--soft);padding-top:4px;
}
.srcitem .what{font-size:14.5px;}
.srcitem .what b{font-weight:600;}
footer{margin-top:64px;padding-top:20px;border-top:1px solid var(--line);}
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="wrap">

  <header class="mast">
    <h1>Catching Vault–BRV control failures before they become exceptions</h1>
    <p class="standfirst">A phased proposal to put a prediction layer alongside two Business Rules Validation controls — ABC and counterparty validation — scoring trades at creation, grouping alerts by root cause, and proving its accuracy in shadow before anyone is asked to rely on it.</p>
  </header>

  <section>
    <div class="ask">
      <span class="tag">The ask, up front</span>
      <p class="big">We are not asking you to trust a model. We are asking for four weeks to measure what the controls already do.</p>
      <p>Phase 1 uses alert history we already hold and people we already have. Nothing changes in production. It answers four questions: how many alerts fire, how many are real, how often the same cause repeats, and how many could have been caught earlier. If the answers do not show a problem worth solving, we stop there and it has cost nothing.</p>
      <p>Every later phase has a number attached to it, agreed with the control owner before that phase starts. We do not move on until the number is met.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="sechead">
      <span class="kicker">Scope</span>
      <h2>Two controls, chosen to test two different answers</h2>
      <p class="lede">The pair is deliberate. One will show whether a simple fix is enough. The other will show whether a model is actually needed. Either way the pilot gives a useful answer.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="grid2">
      <div class="card">
        <span class="no">CONTROL ONE</span>
        <h3>ABC — active book check</h3>
        <p>Checks that the book a trade is booked to is active. High volume, and the answer is always a clear yes or no. The cause is usually sitting in reference data before the trade even exists. We picked it to test the cheap answer: if simply watching book status gets most of the benefit, no model is needed, and we will say so.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <span class="no">CONTROL TWO</span>
        <h3>Counterparty validation</h3>
        <p>Checks the counterparty against ISD static data, using GRID ID, BERID and related identifiers. Here the answer is not always clear. A counterparty can arrive under a different spelling of its name, at the wrong level of a group, or against a record that was only half set up. Working out which legal entity was actually meant is a matching job — and matching is the one thing a model does better than a rule.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="note" style="margin-top:14px;"><b>Why the pair matters.</b> A pilot on one control only tells you whether that control got better. These two tell you something more useful: which kind of control is worth this treatment, and which is better fixed by sorting out the reference data. That is the answer that decides whether there is a programme here at all.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="sechead">
      <span class="kicker">Scope guardrails</span>
      <h2>Four things this proposal will not do</h2>
      <p class="lede">These are commitments, not aspirations. They are what make the rest of the proposal reviewable.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="grid2">
      <div class="card">
        <span class="no">01</span>
        <h3>No alert is ever suppressed</h3>
        <p>The model never closes, hides, downgrades or filters an alert. Every rule fires exactly as it does today and every exception reaches its owning team. The model can only add information to an alert that already exists.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <span class="no">02</span>
        <h3>The rules engine stays the control of record</h3>
        <p>BRV logic is untouched. No model output is written back into the rules engine, and no threshold changes as a side effect of a prediction. The control evidenced to Audit is the same control.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <span class="no">03</span>
        <h3>Every prediction carries reason codes</h3>
        <p>A score with no explanation is unusable in a control function. Each output names the fields that drove it and the comparable history behind it, traceable to source records. Interpretable models first; no deep learning in the pilot.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <span class="no">04</span>
        <h3>A human makes every decision</h3>
        <p>The model ranks and explains. An analyst disposes. Accountability for the control stays with the control owner at every phase, including anything we have not asked for yet.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="sechead">
      <span class="kicker">The first question</span>
      <h2>We already have these controls. What is the model adding?</h2>
      <p class="lede">Neither control is deficient and nothing here improves its detection. ABC tests whether a book is active; counterparty validation tests a trade against ISD. Both do what they were written to do. The gap is not in what they detect — it is in everything a control is structurally unable to hold.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="ask" style="margin-bottom:22px;">
      <span class="tag">The whole answer in one line</span>
      <p class="big">The rule knows the policy. It does not know the history.</p>
      <p>A control has no memory, and that is by design. It checks one trade, against one condition, at one moment, and then forgets. It does not know it raised two hundred alerts on the same book last month. It does not know how any of them were resolved. And it cannot see a cause that exists before the trade does. Everything we are proposing is built from that history — which the control itself can never use.</p>
    </div>

    <figure style="margin-top:22px;">
      <div class="figscroll narrow">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 920 400" role="img" aria-label="A control checks one trade, against one condition, at one moment, then forgets. Three things it has no memory of are shown as empty dashed boxes on the left, and the same three things are shown as held by the history on the right: two hundred alerts on the same book last month, how each was resolved, and the book going inactive at 09:14 before the trade existed.">
          <rect class="nk" x="20" y="20" width="880" height="56" rx="3"/>
          <text class="tnow" x="460" y="54" style="font-size:15px;font-weight:600">A control checks one trade, against one condition, at one moment — then forgets.</text>

          <path class="bnd" d="M470,96 V356"/>
          <text class="cap" x="230" y="118" text-anchor="middle">WHAT THE CONTROL KNOWS</text>
          <text class="capa" x="700" y="118" text-anchor="middle">WHAT THE HISTORY KNOWS</text>

          <rect class="absent" x="20" y="136" width="420" height="62" rx="3"/>
          <text class="tmid" x="230" y="174">no memory of it</text>
          <rect class="ai" x="500" y="136" width="400" height="62" rx="3"/>
          <text class="tnow" x="700" y="162">200 alerts raised on this same book</text>
          <text class="tnow" x="700" y="182">in the last month</text>

          <rect class="absent" x="20" y="212" width="420" height="62" rx="3"/>
          <text class="tmid" x="230" y="250">no record of it</text>
          <rect class="ai" x="500" y="212" width="400" height="62" rx="3"/>
          <text class="tnow" x="700" y="238">how every one of them was resolved</text>
          <text class="tnow" x="700" y="258">187 were the same routine rebooking</text>

          <rect class="absent" x="20" y="288" width="420" height="62" rx="3"/>
          <text class="tmid" x="230" y="326">cannot see it</text>
          <rect class="ai" x="500" y="288" width="400" height="62" rx="3"/>
          <text class="tnow" x="700" y="314">the book went inactive at 09:14</text>
          <text class="tnow" x="700" y="334">hours before the trade existed</text>

          <text class="tnow" x="460" y="386" style="font-size:13px">Everything we are proposing is built from the right-hand column.</text>
        </svg>
      </div>
      <figcaption>The left column is not a criticism of the control. It is what a control is: a test, not a record. The right column already exists in the alert history — it is simply not available to anything that makes a decision.</figcaption>
    </figure>

    <div class="tblwrap">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>The control does this</th><th>It cannot do this</th><th>So today it falls to</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Checks the trade in front of it, at the moment it runs</td><td>Warn you at 09:14 that every trade on that book is going to fail tonight</td><td>Nobody, unless someone happens to spot it</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Raises one alert for every trade that fails</td><td>Notice that 200 of those alerts are the same book and the same single fix</td><td>An experienced analyst who recognises the pattern</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Says pass or fail</td><td>Say which failures matter — a real problem, or a routine rebooking it has already seen fifty times</td><td>Analyst judgement, in whatever order the queue happens to be in</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Matches the counterparty identifier exactly as it arrives</td><td>Work out that a slightly different name, or a parent used instead of a subsidiary, meant one particular GRID ID</td><td>A manual lookup in ISD, one entity at a time</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Applies the same test to every trade</td><td>Tell you that most of its own alerts close as no issue, or that another rule is duplicating it</td><td>A periodic review, if one happens</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Sends the exception to the team that owns the rule</td><td>Send it to the team that owns the cause, which for both of these is usually static data rather than trading</td><td>Reassignment, after the first team has already looked at it</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <p class="note" style="margin-top:16px;"><b>Look down the third column.</b> The gap is already being closed — by what your most experienced people carry in their heads. That works, but it is different from one analyst to the next, it is not available to a new joiner, it is thinner on a Friday evening, and it leaves when they do. We are not proposing to replace that judgement. We are proposing to write it down so the queue can use it.</p>

    <h3 style="margin:36px 0 2px;">The same day, twice</h3>
    <p class="lede">One book moved to inactive-pending at 09:14. Six trades were booked to it before anyone noticed.</p>
    <div class="vs">
      <div class="col now">
        <h4>Today</h4>
        <div class="tl">
          <div class="ev"><time>09:14</time><span>Book CF-2291 set to inactive-pending in reference data. No one downstream is told.</span></div>
          <div class="ev"><time>09:20</time><span>Trading continues. Six trades are booked to it through the day.</span></div>
          <div class="ev"><time>18:30</time><span>ABC fires six times. Every alert is correct.</span></div>
          <div class="ev"><time>next day</time><span>Six exceptions are worked, possibly by different people, each investigated from scratch. Five were a routine rebooking, one was a genuine late trade that nobody has yet separated from the other five.</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="col next">
        <h4>With the layer</h4>
        <div class="tl">
          <div class="ev"><time>09:14</time><span>The status change is picked up.</span></div>
          <div class="ev"><time>09:20</time><span>One item appears in the fix queue: this book, this change, open flow against it, here is what happened the last fourteen times.</span></div>
          <div class="ev"><time>by 11:00</time><span>Ops confirms with the desk and rebooks. Five of the six never become exceptions.</span></div>
          <div class="ev"><time>18:30</time><span>ABC fires once, on the genuine late trade — which is now the only thing anyone has to investigate.</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="note" style="margin-top:16px;"><b>Say this part out loud too.</b> For a deterministic control like ABC, a good deal of that left-hand column is fixed by watching reference data, which is a rule rather than a model. If Phase 1 shows a simple ISD and book-status watch captures most of the value, that is what we will recommend, and it will be cheaper than what we came in with. The model earns its keep on counterparty validation, where the question is not whether a record matched but which entity was meant — a matching problem with name variants, group hierarchies and incomplete onboarding in it, and one that a rule can only ever answer exactly or not at all.</p>
  </section>

